        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "72795916-d0e6-584d-bc5c-f734f0a07d7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrey Zvyagintsev, Marvin Heemeyer, Naboth, a King, a Queen\n- Works: Leviathan (2014 film)\n- Places: United States, Russia, Granby, Colorado\n- Concepts: Naboth's Vineyard, adaptation, inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- On June 4, 2004, Marvin Heemeyer drove an armored bulldozer through Granby, Colorado, damaging 13 buildings and causing about $7 million in damage.\n- Andrey Zvyagintsev said that Marvin Heemeyer's story in the United States inspired Leviathan and that he adapted it into a Russian setting.\n- Critics compared Leviathan more closely to the biblical story of Naboth's Vineyard, in which a King seeks a subject's land and his Queen encourages him to obtain it slyly.",
